    "12_Redcedar_dead_selected.csv": {
      "Longitude": "-124.1632",
      "Latitude": "47.1316",
      "CoordConf": "A",
      "CoordBasis": "Leaning tree on bank, conspicuous on georeferenced airphotos",
      "Estuary": "Copalis River",
      "FieldID": "GF2",
      "TrunkSamp": "25-May-1995",
      "TrunkOutYr": "1675",
      "RootSamp": "31-May-1994",
      "RootBarkYr": "1699",
      "RootTop": "-0.8",
      "RootBot": "-1.2",
      "RingCount": "255",
      "InnerRing": "1368",
      "BuriedSoil": "On 27-Jun-1997, observed in cleaned bank as sandy gray mud without organic horizon, but containing sawed root in growth position, with bark preserved on lower one-third of its exterior. Top of buried soil 1.0 m below tidal-marsh surface at top of cleaned bank (BA, CJu, JCM, JW, SB) ",
      "RootObserv": "BA BB CJu GJ JCM JW SB",
      "Comments": "Bark-bearing root sawed as UC-DC-3, one slice 12 cm thick, 31-May-1994 (GJ, BB). Trunk sampled as GF-2, tag 60 (recorded 27-Jun-1997 as tag 50), in three cores 25-May-1995, for pattern match with sawed root (GJ, BB). Earliest sampled ring 1368 in root GF2RTB. Trunk standing but leaning from river bank during both these visits and on 27-Jun-1997, when stratigraphy at sawed root observed (BA, CJu, JCM, JW, SB). Trunk fell into river in first few years thereafter. Sawed-root elevations were referenced both to modern tidal marsh above (depth 0.9-1.3 m) and to an estimate of local MHHW (0.8-1.2 m). The local estimate of MHHW was based on leveling to a high but ebbing tide on 11-Sep-1996 (predicted level at Aberdeen 0.3 m below MHHW there) measured near tree 789. The levels at GF2 and 789 were related by leveling 27-Jun-1997 with closure error 7 cm to a bench mark set 11-Sep-1996 beside tree 789 (BA, CJu). Notes for tree 789 describe a later cross-check, on 29-Dec-1997, of this Copalis MHHW. "
    }
  },
